      "title": "ElizaOS Community Discussion - July 3, 2026",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "In the general discussion channel, community members expressed frustration over the perceived lack of communication from the ElizaOS team. One user questioned whether the project was dead due to an absence of news, while another noted that the $elizaOS token appeared to be ignored. A community member responded that the project is still alive and building, though this response was criticized as arrogant and unhelpful by another user who pointed out that the official X account had not posted since May, the chat was largely inactive, and the token price was hitting new all-time lows. A debate followed about the appropriate way to address community concerns, with one participant clarifying they were not part of the staff. One user specifically praised Odilitime as the only team-adjacent member who had consistently provided accurate information in a polite and respectful manner since the original team split. Separately, a link was shared to a post by shawmakesmagic that generated brief discussion, with one user noting the post was actually a reply to an older message from November 2024 rather than recent content.",
